Here's a simple CSS code snippet to customize the font size of the page header with the class `.header`:

```css
.header {
  font-size: 24px; /* You can adjust the size as needed */
}
```

### Explanation:
- `.header` is the selector targeting the element with the class `header`.
- `font-size: 24px;` sets the font size to 24 pixels. You can change this value to any valid font size (e.g., `1.5em`, `1rem`, `16px`, etc.).

### Optional: Add more styling
If you want to customize other aspects of the header as well, you can extend the CSS like this:

```css
.header {
  font-size: 24px;
  font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif;
  color: #333;
  text-align: center;
  margin: 20px 0;
}
```

